{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/78530-abyssal-resonance-as-a-managable-curse","id":78530,"title":"Abyssal Resonance as a managable curse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-24T13:06:22-08:00","id":78530,"title":"Abyssal Resonance as a managable curse","content":"Occasionally, I ponder Abyssals and how Resonance could be better. Part of my problem with it is that I mostly like how Resonance normally operates. I like the idea that because the Abyssal agreed to kill the world, he can do it by accident - he has to actively try not to kill the world if he wants to try to be a hero. What I've never liked is that, if your Storyteller is strict about following the Resonance rules and you are playing a &quot;heroic&quot; Abyssal, you should be suffering involuntary Resonance eruptions quite often - far more often than other Exalts suffer Limit Break. Trying to manage Resonance with voluntary eruptions is either incapacitating from overuse of Stigmata, incredibly destructive to the surrounding environment and your own plans (a win for the Neverborn), or trivialized by bleeding Stigmata and rapidly regenerating the damage through Medicine and Resistance Charms. The middle one can be playable, if you are doing the &quot;redemption into a Solar because woe-is-me-I'm-an-Abyssal&quot; story, but the first is too hard and the last is too easy.<br /> <br /> I had a thought on the problem. What if Resonance was a thing that Abyssals had to hold back? There's all sorts of fiction where a character has some sort of curse he has to protect the world from. The classic example is the werewolf. He's got a monster inside him that wants to kill and maim others and he can't cure himself, but he can take steps to keep that curse from hurting others. He can get as far away from people as he can or chain himself in his basement. Depending on the style of lycanthropy, there could be some method by which he can prevent the change or at least gain some control over his actions while transformed, a potion he can take maybe or simply pitting his willpower against that of the monster. If Resonance functioned upon a similar narrative track, it would be this periodic disaster that an Abyssal could take steps to either mitigate or prevent.<br /> <br /> In essence, Resonance would function more like Infernal Limit. Loyalist Abyssals could just skip fighting Resonance or even use it to their own advantage (Resonance Ben, anyone?), redemption seekers can still have reason to become Solars, and other Abyssals can find ways to live with what they are. The methods could even vary from Abyssal to Abyssal. Perhaps one finds that an ascetic lifestyle allows him to keep Resonance eruptions from occurring while a different Abyssal doesn't get any benefit from the same, but a periodic murder spree keeps him from killing whole cities by accident.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T13:52:26-08:00","id":78558,"title":"","content":"It's not out of the question, depending on your table, to say that Abyssals can learn how to purposefully vent Resonance to deal with it to match that the player is choosing when it occurs. Though I would think that this would be on the path to redemption or just coming to grips with the Black Exaltation.<br /> <br /> One additional factor to consider is that eruptions that don't really inconvenience the Abyssal are also a no-no as far as the book is concerned. So always running off to the same area to blow off your Blight (if you can control it in the first place) has an additional RAW problem.<br /> <br /> It really depends on what you want the power dynamics of the Abyssal condition to have. As written, it's a chain that there's not much way around. If you wanted to change that, I don't think it would be problematic as long as you understand how that changes the role of Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T14:29:14-08:00","id":78609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wednesday</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/78530-abyssal-resonance-as-a-managable-curse?p=78558#post78558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One additional factor to consider is that eruptions that don't really inconvenience the Abyssal are also a no-no as far as the book is concerned. So always running off to the same area to blow off your Blight (if you can control it in the first place) has an additional RAW problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that I had an implicit assumption in what I said above that Loyalist Abyssals shouldn't mind Resonance eruptions in general. Sure, it sucks if they are trying to go deep cover in Lookshy to suddenly be surrounded by spectral ghost images and having all nearby plants wither and die, but when you are leading an army of the undead in an assault on Lookshy's walls, those ghostly images and dying plants are just icing on the cake.<br /> <br /> I suppose this vision of Resonance I'm seeing has Resonance as a black gift from the Neverborn, a boon to their loyal servants and a bane to Creation. As a general rule, Loyalists would want Resonance to accrue, Renegades wouldn't, and others are conflicted. Consider the possibilities - If Resonance gives you a Midas' touch like quality, causing everything you touch to turn to sterile grave dust, that's a potent weapon at the right time, but at others turns you into an obviously dangerous monster. Charms could have costs that give you points of Resonance - something Loyalists would love to get but would cause Renegades to avoid them like the plague. Likewise, behaviors that would cause a Renegade to lose points of Resonance would be performed often, while Loyalists would do whatever they could to dodge the issue.<br /> <br /> Resonance eruptions could become really cool 'apocalypse' events, where things like the sun being swallowed by darkness and hungry ghosts rising in the daytime could happen, possibly as personalized as a Solar's Limit Break.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It really depends on what you want the power dynamics of the Abyssal condition to have. As written, it's a chain that there's not much way around. If you wanted to change that, I don't think it would be problematic as long as you understand how that changes the role of Abyssals. </div> </div> </div>Resonance right now forces a split - you are either a Loyalist by choice or by inaction, or you are a Renegade eventually seeking redemption into a Solar. These are the only viable character arcs for Abyssals. You can't really be in rebellion against the Neverborn and not try to avoid Resonance, not without being inconsistent with the character's motivations, and you can't just sit out the conflict because Resonance throws in on the side of Loyalists. There is no third option. I want Abyssals to have third options, whatever form they take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T14:30:58-08:00","id":78615,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for Resonance earlier that would replace it with an Abyssal &quot;Dark Fate&quot;.<br /> <br /> The idea is that each Abyssal shard bears a curse (which is the Great Curse twisted and inverted by Abyssal essence.) Rather than affecting them like the Solar Great Curse, the Abyssal Great Curse affects the world around them, causing each Abyssal to be followed by a particular sort of misfortune. You choose the type of curse at chargen (like Solars do.) Curses are basically broad &quot;plot hooks&quot; -- for example, an Abyssal might be cursed to be followed by warfare wherever they go. When your Limit-equivalent breaks, something happens somewhere vaguely near you that pushes the world towards what you're cursed with. Curses are vague &quot;the plot is biased towards this direction&quot; rather than one specific event -- it doesn't manifest as obvious mechanical things, but as freak coincidences. These coincidences tend to be freakish enough to seem unnatural, and people become intuitively aware on a gut level that the Abyssal is responsible, so they end up blamed for the misfortune that follows them.<br /> <br /> But here's the fun part: When your Dark Fate breaks, you receive an instant vision of the impending misfortune -- a vision of the message that will go awry and cause a chain of events leading to a horrific war, or the accident that will claim the life of someone vital to maintaining the peace, or something of that nature. And there's always enough time to at least try and avert it, although you may have to pay great costs, take risks, sacrifice whatever you're currently working on, etc. This allows heroic Abyssals to be be haunted and cursed (which is true for all the Exalted), while still giving them regular chances to behave heroically.<br /> <br /> The fact that you choose your curse is important. (Imagine if every Solar <i>had</i> to take Berserk Anger or Heart of Tears-- they're very thematic and important curses to offer as options, but if you were forced to take something like that it would ruin countless character concepts.)<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is... in general, I think the issue isn't making Resonance manageable (although of course it does have to be.) The core issue is that Resonance should be <i>fun</i>, in a way that adds to the game rather than limiting it. Solar Limit Breaks tend to be Very Bad things when they happen, but people don't resent them nearly as much because they were chosen at chargen (so they tend to fit your character) and because, generally, many of them allow you to look cool even as you're flipping out in horrible ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-24-2014, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T14:43:05-08:00","id":78628,"title":"","content":"@Kyeundo -- Alright, I see what you are saying now. You're looking for Resonance to be something other than the displeasure of the Neverborn (unless the Loyalists are intentionally pissing them off to get Resonance effects). This makes the current eruptions very problematic however, as every single Loyalist would be banking Resonance to try and get instant Shadowland or &quot;I'm possessed by the Neverborn, take that unnatural mental influence and shove it&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's not a bad idea at all. It's just a very fundamental shift in the nature of the idea of Resonance. It's no longer a punishment (by definition) at all. I like Aquillon's idea, especially when they mention the idea of the instant vision of misfortune. It would give Loyalists something to work towards and Renegades something to work against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T14:56:06-08:00","id":78655,"title":"","content":"I once made a dusk caste inspired by Joan of Arc. She had whispers 5 and tried to prevent the &quot;visions&quot; that she received from coming to pass. She was a lot of fun to play, and I would love it if resonance in 3e worked as Aquillion described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:16:08-08:00","id":78677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/78530-abyssal-resonance-as-a-managable-curse?p=78615#post78615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea for Resonance earlier that would replace it with an Abyssal &quot;Dark Fate&quot;.<br /> <br /> The idea is that each Abyssal shard bears a curse (which is the Great Curse twisted and inverted by Abyssal essence.) Rather than affecting them like the Solar Great Curse, the Abyssal Great Curse affects the world around them, causing each Abyssal to be followed by a particular sort of misfortune. You choose the type of curse at chargen (like Solars do.) Curses are basically broad &quot;plot hooks&quot; -- for example, an Abyssal might be cursed to be followed by warfare wherever they go. When your Limit-equivalent breaks, something happens somewhere vaguely near you that pushes the world towards what you're cursed with. Curses are vague &quot;the plot is biased towards this direction&quot; rather than one specific event -- it doesn't manifest as obvious mechanical things, but as freak coincidences. These coincidences tend to be freakish enough to seem unnatural, and people become intuitively aware on a gut level that the Abyssal is responsible, so they end up blamed for the misfortune that follows them.<br /> <br /> But here's the fun part: When your Dark Fate breaks, you receive an instant vision of the impending misfortune -- a vision of the message that will go awry and cause a chain of events leading to a horrific war, or the accident that will claim the life of someone vital to maintaining the peace, or something of that nature. And there's always enough time to at least try and avert it, although you may have to pay great costs, take risks, sacrifice whatever you're currently working on, etc. This allows heroic Abyssals to be be haunted and cursed (which is true for all the Exalted), while still giving them regular chances to behave heroically.<br /> <br /> The fact that you choose your curse is important. (Imagine if every Solar <i>had</i> to take Berserk Anger or Heart of Tears-- they're very thematic and important curses to offer as options, but if you were forced to take something like that it would ruin countless character concepts.)<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is... in general, I think the issue isn't making Resonance manageable (although of course it does have to be.) The core issue is that Resonance should be <i>fun</i>, in a way that adds to the game rather than limiting it. Solar Limit Breaks tend to be Very Bad things when they happen, but people don't resent them nearly as much because they were chosen at chargen (so they tend to fit your character) and because, generally, many of them allow you to look cool even as you're flipping out in horrible ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get part of what you are saying - if you can choose your doom, it feels more manageable as a player because you signed up for that particular problem. You thought you could handle that at character creation and you already have ideas about what to do with it. I don't like the implementation so much, though, because it feels like Stealing the Spotlight Prana. Every time your Resonance goes off, your horrible vision becomes the new plot hook and the story becomes all about stopping the terrible event your existence caused. With a Solar Limit Break, the problem itself might be over in a single scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wednesday</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/78530-abyssal-resonance-as-a-managable-curse?p=78628#post78628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Kyeundo -- Alright, I see what you are saying now. You're looking for Resonance to be something other than the displeasure of the Neverborn (unless the Loyalists are intentionally pissing them off to get Resonance effects). This makes the current eruptions very problematic however, as every single Loyalist would be banking Resonance to try and get instant Shadowland or &quot;I'm possessed by the Neverborn, take that unnatural mental influence and shove it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance would need a major overhaul to go alongside this and its interpretation would change alongside it. Resonance would no longer be about punishing transgressing Abyssals - it would be a manifestation of the Neverborn's power, channeled through the Abyssal. I like the idea of personalizing it to the Abyssal. One might cause nearby rivers and bodies of water to turn to blood, another might rip open a shadowland, and a third might cause a zombie apocalypse. Resonance would be a thing that accrues over time as well as something that you can gain and lose through Charms and actions, and gaining more would be a matter of affirming the Neverborn's goals instead of resisting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}